t year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 8% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 21% and a beta of 0.47, it is more defensive than the market, though its beta has shifted (1y -0.11 vs 5y 0.40), so read it loosely.","About $24.1M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 49% in the 2020 crash, 21% in the 2022 bear market and 51% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades 56% below its DCF fair value of $97.90, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 32%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $59.95 to $159 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","Multiples send mixed signals against Real Estate peers: cheaper on P/E 4.4 vs 23.9, richer on EV/EBITDA 22.4 vs 16.2 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 31% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 5.3% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 6.1% (vs the 8% bar).","The 7 covering analysts target $48.00 on average, 11% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 5% falls short of the cost of capital of 6.7%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.34).","It converts 49% of revenue into free cash flow, or 45% after stock compensation.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.15x.","AFFO margin (a proxy for distributable REIT cash) is 49%.","ROE of 11% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.9x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 23pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 3.4x net debt to EBITDA ($14.4M of cash against $842.2M of debt), with interest covered 6.2x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 14.5% over 3 years, 10.5% over 5 years and 6.8% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating.","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 3.3% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Margins are expanding (+1.9% trend).","Forward indicators: FFO growth of 3.2% a year over five years.","Capex runs only 0.2x depreciation (2.8% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 2.0%, and institutions hold 81%.","Insider trading is two-way: 5 purchases and 1 sale over the past year, net $643K bought.","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.3% (5.3% in dividends, less 4.1% of net share issuance).","The share count has grown 6.8% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It has paid a dividend for 24 consecutive years, raising it 3.5% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 25 employees, each generates about $10.5M of revenue, 4.6x the Real Estate median, and revenue has grown 8.4% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $5.1M of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.8M (0x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $373K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":67,"head":"Watch: composite 45, above the 39 line, but it earns less than its cost of capital.","pros":["Composite 45, above the 39 line (gates 12/26)","Trades 56% below fair value of $97.90","FCF margin 49.0%","Revenue grew 10.5%/yr over 5y","P/E 4.4x vs sector 23.9x"],"cons":["ROIC 5.5% vs WACC 6.7%","Net debt/EBITDA 3.4x","EV/EBITDA 22.4x vs sector 16.2x"],"flags":[],"need":["it earns less than its cost of capital"],"buy_below":83.22,"vc":{"base":97.9,"base_src":"dcf","bear":59.95,"bull":158.58,"alt_median":54.11,"n_alt":3,"gap":1.6874,"dispersion":0.3231,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (32% dispersion)","DCF is 169% above the other models' median ($54.11)"]},"med":{"pe":23.8785,"ev_ebitda":16.1705,"pfcf":17.849,"pb":1.3551,"roic":0.0405,"gross_margin"